leios.system.base-files (1.0.1) stable; urgency=medium

  * preinst: register diversions with --no-rename instead of --rename to
    avoid dpkg-divert's "dangerous" warning when diverting files owned by
    an essential package (/usr/lib/os-release, /etc/issue, /etc/issue.net).
    --add is idempotent, so existing systems already diverged with the old
    --rename rule are not disturbed.
  * postrm: keep --remove --rename so the original essential-package files
    are restored on removal for systems that had them moved aside, while
    remaining a clean no-op on new --no-rename systems.

 -- Linus Fischer <leicraft@leicraftmc.de>  Sun, 9 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0200

leios.system.base-files (1.0.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.

